{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC4 follow-up landed. The completion verifier correctly flagged that my first AC4 evidence was factually wrong: the `review-bot` compose service had NO healthcheck (only `mcp` did), so nothing at the container layer distinguished the zombie (\"listener closed, process alive\") from healthy — that absence is exactly why the 2026-08-28 state was silent for 22 minutes.\n\nFixed honestly by ADDING the missing signal rather than re-wording the evidence:\n\n- Gerrit change 2384 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2384) — MERGED, LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 (CI run 33269891017, py3.11/3.12/3.13 + macos all green).\n- Adds a per-container `healthcheck:` to the `review-bot` service in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`, probing the process's OWN listener over container loopback at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/health`. In the zombie state uvicorn has closed that listener → connection refused → probe exits non-zero → after `retries` the container flips to **unhealthy**, an observable/alarmable signal.\n- Reporting-only, so it does NOT change the recreate contract: `autodeploy.sh` runs `docker compose up -d` WITHOUT `--wait` and gates on its own curl `/health` probe; `restart: unless-stopped` does not act on health status. This kept it a localized observability fix, not a lifecycle/design change (so no escalation was warranted).\n- RED→GREEN regression test `test_reviewbot_healthcheck_probes_its_own_listener` asserts the stanza exists and probes the bot's own `127.0.0.1:8000/health` listener; sandboxed mutation check caught all three mutants (wrong port, wrong path, removed stanza).\n\nTogether with the merged force-exit fix (change 2381, commit a36c7407), all five acceptance criteria are now met: the zombie state is both DETECTED (this healthcheck) and BOUNDED (the force-exit self-terminates it within the stop grace, releasing the port)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788031593779511713,"uuid":"225e9212-8878-4fa3-9efd-13d4ffc88cb4"}